-- title:
--   Integrality of the quotient B₀/(ξ_B-a)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, a positive integer $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity admitting a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi)=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField` of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ for the subgroup `levelH` $(q\ell)\,M'$, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ whose maximal ideal contains $q$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\to L$, and let $j\in K$ be a nonzero element whose Laurent series is the coefficient embedding of $jq$. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(q)$, such that $A$ and $K$ are $A_0$-algebras in a scalar tower, $A$ is module-finite over $A_0$, and $A=A_0[\zeta_A]$ for some $\zeta_A$ whose image in $L$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity; assume $A_0$ contains a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity and that $\ell$ and $M'$ are units in $A_0$. Assume further: the stability of level-$\ell$ Katz structures and of $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-kernel polynomials under Weierstrass variable change over all $A_0$-algebras; a family $\mathcal{G}$ of relative group laws on projective Weierstrass models with unit discriminant which is chord-tangent and has the origin as identity; a level transport $\mathcal{T}$ for Drinfeld $q$-bases which is a section transport; and the existence of graded ring homomorphisms on the projective models realising variable changes and coefficient changes. Let $P_0$ be an abstract moduli package for the rigid Weierstrass datum `rigidDataPow`, i.e. a ring $B_0$ over $A_0$ with a universal point such that each point over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ comes from a unique $A_0$-algebra map $B_0\to T$. Let $\xi_B\in B_0$ satisfy $\Phi_\ell(\xi_B)=0$, assume $B_0/(\xi_B-\mathrm{algebraMap}\,a)$ is nontrivial for every $a\in A_0$ with $a^\ell=1$, $a\ne 1$, and assume that at every field-valued point $y$ over a field $F$ with $\ell\ne 0$ in $F$ the classifying map sends $\xi_B$ to a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity. Finally let $x$ be a point of the moduli problem over $K$ whose $j$-invariant has Laurent series `jqNModC L (q * ℓ)`. Then for every $a\in A_0$ with $a^\ell=1$ and $a\ne 1$, the quotient $B_0/(\xi_B-\mathrm{algebraMap}\,a)$ is an integral domain.
--
--   This identifies the $\ell$-Weil-pairing eigenquotients of the coordinate ring of the full-level moduli problem (level $\Gamma_0(M')$-power, level-$\ell$ Katz structure and Drinfeld $q$-basis) as integral domains, the algebraic counterpart of the irreducibility of the corresponding components of the modular curve. It feeds the description of the minimal primes of $B_0$ as the ideals $(\xi_B - a)$.
